# Allodium developer console — local configuration.
#
# Copy to .env.local and edit. docs/getting-started.md has the whole walkthrough,
# including a one-line Docker command for a database to point this at.
#
# The console is a localhost-only tool in v1: no authentication, binds the loopback
# interface, refuses cross-origin writes. Do not expose it.
# It serves on 3180 to stay clear of whatever you already run on 3000.

# The database the console reads and writes. These values match the Docker command in
# docs/getting-started.md — change them to match the database you actually created.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://allodium:localdev@localhost:5433/allodium_dev

# Where @allodium/storage keeps uploaded bytes. File metadata lives in your files
# table, where foreign keys can reach it. Defaults to <app>/.uploads when unset.
# UPLOADS_DIR=

# OPTIONAL, recommended: a SELECT-only role for the SQL console, so its read-only
# guarantee rests on database privileges rather than on session settings a query could
# change. Created by dev/seed/004-readonly-role.sql. Without it the SQL console falls
# back to the main role and says so in its footer.
CONSOLE_RO_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://allodium_ro:readonly@localhost:5433/allodium_dev

# OPTIONAL: masking overrides — comma-separated "table.column", or a bare "column" to
# match that name in every table. Columns whose names look like credentials are masked
# automatically; these adjust that judgement in either direction.
# CONSOLE_MASK_EXTRA=customers.notes
# CONSOLE_MASK_EXEMPT=orders.token_type
